# Grants the active login session's user dynamic ACL access to keyboard event nodes.
# The same "uaccess" mechanism systemd-udev already uses for joysticks (see /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-uaccess.rules),
# extended here to keyboards.
#
# This is needed because affiro's `monitor` command reads raw keyboard input directly under Wayland, where no portal API
# can deliver a stream of ordinary keystrokes.
# Keyboard event nodes are deliberately excluded from udev's built-in uaccess rule, since ordinary unprivileged
# keylogging is exactly what that exclusion guards against.
# Installing this rule is an explicit, informed opt-in to that access for affiro.

SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
